== Electromagnetism

#statement("Theorem", title: [Curl-less(irrotational) fields])[
The following are equivalent

- $"curl" upright(bold(F)) = nabla times upright(bold(F)) = 0$

- $integral_a^b upright(bold(F)) d upright(bold(l))$ is the independent of the path, for given end points

- $integral.cont upright(bold(F)) d upright(bold(l)) = 0$ for any closed loop

- $upright(bold(F)) = - nabla V$ for some potential $V$ which is unique up to a constant

]
#statement("Theorem", title: [Divergence-less(solenoidal) fields])[
The following are equivalent

- $"div" upright(bold(F)) = nabla upright(bold(F)) = 0$

- $integral.double upright(bold(F)) d upright(bold(a))$ is the independent of the path, for given boundary line

- $integral.surf upright(bold(F)) d upright(bold(a)) = 0$ for any closed surface

- $upright(bold(F)) = "curl" upright(bold(A))$, unique up to a gradient of any scalar function

]
